{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For</b> — the deeds of HaShem, corresponding to their deed." "<b>Nor the work of His hands</b> — corresponding to \"like the work of their hands.\" The meaning: if they had understood the deeds of HaShem, they would not have wrought iniquity, for they would have known that HaShem will destroy them. And some say: that this is a prayer, or a mode of prophecy, and the meaning of \"He will not build them up\" is that they shall fall and rise no more."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:48.236799191Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}